\section{Conclusion}
Donec nec justo eget felis aliquet bibendum. Sed non risus. Praesent vitae sapien at nisl consectetur ultrices.

\end{document}
```

In this example, we've included the `hyperref` package to enable clickable links in the TOC. The `\tableofcontents` command should be placed before the first section heading. The TOC will be automatically generated based on the section headings in the document.

When you compile this document, you should see a table of contents like this:

```
Table of Contents
1. Introduction
2. Body
  2.1. Subsection
3. Conclusion
```

Note that the TOC will only include sections and subsections, not paragraph headings. If you want to include paragraph headings, you can use the `\section*` or `\subsection*` commands to create "dummy" sections that won't appear in the TOC.

